course: dictionary
lesson: 14842
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can mean more than one thing. Ragged is one of them. Its main meaning is old and torn, with holes and loose threads: «The old man wore a ragged coat.»
explain: Ragged can also describe edges, shapes and people. «The rocks made a ragged coastline.» Here ragged means rough and uneven, not smooth. «The poor child was in ragged clothes.» Here it means wearing old, torn clothes.
explain: To find the right meaning, read the words around it. Ask what the thing or person is like. If the coat has holes in it, ragged means torn. If the coastline has many bays and points, ragged means uneven.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «The team played a ragged match» with not well together, uneven and untidy. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: «Ragged» means old and torn, with holes and loose threads.
fact: «Ragged» can mean rough and uneven at the edges, not smooth, as in «ragged clouds».
fact: «Ragged» can mean not well together, untidy or tired, as in «a ragged performance».
fact: «Run ragged» means made very tired.
fact: «Rag» can mean to tease, and «ragged» is its past form, but this use is old-fashioned in the UK.
exercise: «The old man wore a ragged coat with holes in the sleeves.» What does ragged mean here? | Bright and shiny | Warm and new | Very long and heavy | *Old and torn, with holes and loose threads
exercise: «The rocks made a ragged coastline with many bays and points.» What does ragged mean here? | Very busy with boats | Covered in snow | Smooth and straight | *Rough and uneven at the edges
exercise: «The team played a ragged match and lost.» What does ragged suggest? | *Not well together, uneven and untidy | Won easily with great style | Played very slowly on purpose
test: «After the long walk, the children were run ragged.» What does run ragged mean? | Ran in a straight line | *Made very tired | Chased by a dog | Given new shoes
test: «The sky was full of ragged clouds.» Which meaning fits best? | Dark and very heavy | Clean and white | Torn and full of holes | *Rough and uneven at the edges
exam: «The ragged child looked cold in the rain.» What does ragged mean here? | Lost in a crowd | Very clever | *Wearing old, torn clothes | Laughing loudly
